{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":33404319,"ns":0,"title":"Argument from analogy","extract":"Argument from analogy is a special type of inductive argument, where perceived similarities are used as a basis to infer some further similarity that has not been observed yet.  Analogical reasoning is one of the most common methods by which human beings try to understand the world and make decisions.","description":"Logical reasoning method","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}